<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42879" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scaptĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				very ancient town in Latium</i>, now <i>Passerano</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, § 68</span></i>.
			—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scaptĭus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
				<i>of Scaptia</i>, <i>Scaptian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					17 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scaptĭensis</span></b> , e,
			adj., <i>of the Scaptian tribe</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribules,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 40</span></i>
			.</div>
